          {
            "author": {
              "__typename": "Bot",
              "login": "greptile-apps"
            },
            "body": "<!-- greptile_summary -->\n\n<h2><a href=\"https://app.greptile.com/api/retrigger?id=70909717\"><picture><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\" srcset=\"https://greptile-static-assets.s3.amazonaws.com/badges/RetriggerDark.svg?v=2\"><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: light)\" srcset=\"https://greptile-static-assets.s3.amazonaws.com/badges/Retrigger.svg?v=2\"><img alt=\"Retrigger\" src=\"https://greptile-static-assets.s3.amazonaws.com/badges/Retrigger.svg?v=2\" align=\"right\"></picture></a>Confidence Score: 4/5</h2>\n\n**[Low risk]** Updates test logic for gradient computation\\.\n\nThe PR appears safe to merge, though the DelayedScaling gradient test still needs a loss scale that exercises its backward GEMMs.\n\n<h2>Findings</h2>\n\n1. <img alt=\"P2\" src=\"https://greptile-static-assets.s3.amazonaws.com/badges/p2.svg?v=9\" align=\"top\">&nbsp;**FP8 gradients become zero** <a href=\"https://github.com/NVIDIA/TransformerEngine/pull/3580#discussion_r4127091186\">▶</a>\n\n<h3>Summary</h3>\n\nThe PR replaces the mean-output loss in the JAX collective LayerNorm MLP gradient tests with a target-based squared-error loss, adds a sharded random target, and updates the gradient helper’s arguments. The new loss still leaves the default DelayedScaling backward GEMM gradients below the initial FP8 quantization range.\n\n<!-- greptile_confidence_score:4 -->\n\n<sub>Reviews (1) · Last reviewed commit: [\"Use target-based loss in collective GEMM...\"](https://github.com/nvidia/transformerengine/commit/1450fb459cb54c12e89d8f2306c66e5c40716f4d)</sub>",
            "createdAt": "2026-09-28T21:13:43Z",
            "databaseId": 5878724666,
            "updatedAt": "2026-09-28T21:14:01Z",
            "url": "https://github.com/NVIDIA/TransformerEngine/pull/3580#issuecomment-5878724666"
          },
          {
            "author": {
